   {:block/created-at 1761790544018,
    :block/updated-at 1761790544018,
    :build/properties {},
    :block/title "Spain Trip November 2025"},
   :blocks
   [{:block/title
     "## 7-Day Spain Itinerary - November 2025\n\n### Trip Overview\n- **Duration:** 7 days\n- **Month:** November\n- **Cities:** Barcelona (3 days) → Madrid (3 days) → Toledo (day trip)\n- **Weather:** Mild temperatures (50-65°F / 10-18°C), less crowded than summer",
     :block/created-at 1761790544061,
     :block/updated-at 1761790544061,
     :build/properties {:logseq.property/heading 2}}
    {:block/title
     "### Day 1-3: Barcelona\n#### Day 1: Gothic Quarter & Las Ramblas\n- Morning: Arrive in Barcelona, check into hotel\n- Afternoon: Explore Gothic Quarter (Barri Gòtic)\n\t- Cathedral of Barcelona\n\t- Plaça Reial\n\t- Walk down Las Ramblas\n- Evening: Dinner in El Born neighborhood\n- **Tip:** Book Sagrada Familia tickets online in advance",
     :block/created-at 1761790549110,
     :block/updated-at 1761790549110,
     :build/properties {:logseq.property/heading 3}}
    {:block/title
     "#### Day 2: Gaudí's Masterpieces\n- Morning: Sagrada Familia (book 9-10am slot)\n- Late Morning: Park Güell (pre-book tickets)\n- Afternoon: Casa Batlló or Casa Milà (La Pedrera)\n- Evening: Passeig de Gràcia shopping and tapas\n- **Note:** November has shorter daylight hours (sunset around 5:30pm)",
     :block/created-at 1761790554292,
     :block/updated-at 1761790554292,
     :build/properties {:logseq.property/heading 4}}
    {:block/title
     "#### Day 3: Montjuïc & Beaches\n- Morning: Montjuïc Castle (cable car or funicular)\n- Midday: Magic Fountain area (show times vary, check schedule)\n- Afternoon: Barceloneta Beach walk (cooler but pleasant)\n- Evening: Seafood dinner in Barceloneta\n- **Travel:** Take evening high-speed train (AVE) to Madrid (2.5-3 hours)",
     :block/created-at 1761790558887,
     :block/updated-at 1761790558887,
     :build/properties {:logseq.property/heading 4}}
    {:block/title
     "### Day 4-6: Madrid\n#### Day 4: Art Triangle\n- Morning: Prado Museum (world-class art collection)\n\t- Velázquez, Goya, El Greco\n- Afternoon: Retiro Park stroll\n- Late Afternoon: Reina Sofía Museum (includes Picasso's Guernica)\n- Evening: Tapas in La Latina neighborhood\n- **Tip:** Museums are less crowded in November",
     :block/created-at 1761790563194,
     :block/updated-at 1761790563194,
     :build/properties {:logseq.property/heading 3}}
    {:block/title
     "#### Day 5: Royal Madrid\n- Morning: Royal Palace of Madrid (largest in Western Europe)\n- Midday: Almudena Cathedral next door\n- Afternoon: Plaza Mayor and Mercado de San Miguel (food market)\n- Late Afternoon: Gran Vía shopping\n- Evening: Flamenco show (book in advance)\n\t- Tablao venues: Corral de la Morería or Casa Patas",
     :block/created-at 1761790568218,
     :block/updated-at 1761790568218,
     :build/properties {:logseq.property/heading 4}}
    {:block/title
     "#### Day 6: Toledo Day Trip\n- Morning: Train to Toledo (30 minutes from Madrid)\n- Full day exploring medieval city:\n\t- Toledo Cathedral\n\t- Alcázar fortress\n\t- El Greco Museum\n\t- Jewish Quarter synagogues\n\t- Winding medieval streets\n- Evening: Return to Madrid for farewell dinner\n- **UNESCO World Heritage Site**",
     :block/created-at 1761790572667,
     :block/updated-at 1761790572667,
     :build/properties {:logseq.property/heading 4}}
    {:block/title
     "### Day 7: Departure\n- Morning: Last-minute souvenir shopping or museum visit\n- Depart from Madrid-Barajas Airport\n\n---\n\n### Essential Travel Tips for Americans\n- **Passport:** Must be valid for at least 3 months beyond departure\n- **Visa:** Not needed for stays under 90 days\n- **Currency:** Euro (€) - credit cards widely accepted\n- **Tipping:** Not mandatory but 5-10% appreciated for good service\n- **Language:** Learn basic Spanish phrases, English spoken in tourist areas\n- **Meal Times:** Lunch 2-4pm, Dinner 9-11pm (later than US!)\n- **Siesta:** Many shops close 2-5pm",
     :block/created-at 1761790578876,
     :block/updated-at 1761790578876,
     :build/properties {:logseq.property/heading 3}}
    {:block/title
     "### What to Pack for November\n- **Layers:** Light jacket, sweaters, long pants\n- **Rain gear:** November can be rainy\n- **Comfortable walking shoes:** Essential!\n- **Power adapter:** European Type C/F plugs (220V)\n- **Day bag:** For carrying water, camera, etc.",
     :block/created-at 1761790583292,
     :block/updated-at 1761790583292,
     :build/properties {:logseq.property/heading 3}}
    {:block/title
     "### Transportation\n- **Between cities:** High-speed AVE trains (book via Renfe.com)\n- **Within cities:** Metro systems excellent in both Barcelona and Madrid\n- **Airport transfers:** \n\t- Barcelona: Aerobus or Metro L9\n\t- Madrid: Metro Line 8 or Airport Express bus",
     :block/created-at 1761790587619,
     :block/updated-at 1761790587619,
     :build/properties {:logseq.property/heading 3}}
    {:block/title
     "### Must-Try Foods\n- **Barcelona:** Paella, pan con tomate, crema catalana\n- **Madrid:** Cocido madrileño, bocadillo de calamares, churros con chocolate\n- **Everywhere:** Jamón ibérico, patatas bravas, tortilla española\n- **Wine:** Rioja, Ribera del Duero, Cava (Spanish sparkling)\n- **Tapas culture:** Small plates meant for sharing",
     :block/created-at 1761790591984,
     :block/updated-at 1761790591984,
     :build/properties {:logseq.property/heading 3}}
    {:block/title
     "### November Advantages\n- ✅ Fewer tourists, shorter lines\n- ✅ Lower hotel prices\n- ✅ Mild, comfortable weather\n- ✅ Authentic local experience\n- ⚠️ Some beach clubs closed\n- ⚠️ Shorter daylight hours\n- ⚠️ Occasional rain (bring umbrella)",
     :block/created-at 1761790598495,
     :block/updated-at 1761790598495,
     :build/properties {:logseq.property/heading 3}}
    {:block/title
     "### Budget Estimate (per person)\n- **Flights:** $500-900 roundtrip\n- **Hotels:** $80-150/night (mid-range)\n- **Food:** $40-60/day\n- **Attractions:** $150-200 total\n- **Transport:** $100-150 (trains, metro)\n- **Total:** ~$1,500-2,500 depending on choices\n\n---\n\n### Booking Checklist\n- [ ] Book flights\n- [ ] Reserve hotels in Barcelona and Madrid\n- [ ] Purchase Sagrada Familia tickets online\n- [ ] Book Park Güell time slot\n- [ ] Reserve flamenco show\n- [ ] Book AVE train Barcelona→Madrid\n- [ ] Get travel insurance\n- [ ] Notify bank of travel dates",
     :block/created-at 1761790604641,
     :block/updated-at 1761790604641,
     :build/properties {:logseq.property/heading 3}}]}
